---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_120",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 120,
  "text": "<p> [[331.22]] <b>105. GEORG HIERONYMUS WELSCH AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[331.23]] Augsburg, [April] 1672.</b></p>\n<p> [[332.6]] Viro Nobil^#'s^#'s^#'o Ampl^#'s^#'s^#'o atque Excell^#'s^#'s^#'o Gothofredo Guilelmo Leibnizio </p>\n<p> [[332.7]] U.J.D. praeclar^#'s^#'s^#'o, Dⁿ^#'o et Fautori suo plurimum honorando, </p>\n<p> [[332.8]] Georgius Hieronymus Velschius S.P.D. </p>\n<p> [[332.9]] Fecisti sane, Vir Nobil^#'s^#'s^#'e atque Ampl^#'s^#'s^#'e, rem Tua benevolentia et constantia amoris dignissimam,\n[[332.10]] quod tardiorem me ad scribendum amice excitaris. Non utar excusatione, ne accusari\n[[332.11]] possim, sed utrisque Tuis jucundissimis eadem opera prolixe respondebo. </p>\n<p> [[332.12]] Nizolium Tua cura editum obiter evolvi. Perplacuit, si Tibi hoc elogii satis fuerit, quo\n[[332.13]] magna omnia complecti soleo. Helvetii experimentum non possum magni facere, etsi vellem in\n[[332.14]] Tui gratiam, quia amicum illum habes. Pertinet enim ad sophismata Chemicorum, nec aliam\n[[332.15]] censuram quisquam peritiorum adferet. Sunt penes me augmentationes ejusmodi plurimae, non\n[[332.16]] fictae, sed operibus commodae, quibus tamen parum delector, nec opus habeo, cum pleraeque\n[[332.17]] panis tantum quotidiani nomine, et operis paupertini, muliebris, ac puerilis extenuatione propemodum\n[[332.18]] infames sint. Nec enim alio referri possunt, quam ad caementationes aurificum, quae\n[[332.19]] Magistratuum sapienti inspectione plerumque mulctis et exilio obnoxiae promulgatae. Reinesii\n[[332.20]] observationes in Medicos vett. exigui momenti sunt, quod ampl^#'s^#'s^#'u^#'s Bosius ipse ad me\n[[332.21]] perscripsit. Dabit tamen nonnulla selectiora in epistolis Medicis ejusdem quae a Philologicis\n[[332.22]] illis Daumii haut parum differunt, si quod promisit, recte intelligo. Jungii <i>phoronomica</i>, si\n[[332.23]] prodierint, multis usui erunt, ut spero. Quae de <i>diariis Gallicis</i> commemorasti, gratissima\n[[332.24]] fuerunt. Acusticum Anglorum multis difficultatibus subjacere videtur. Sonos etiam ventis non\n[[332.25]] impediri Florentini Anglorum aemuli adseruerunt. Sed illis quotidiana experientia opponi\n[[332.26]] potest. </p>\n<p> [[333.1]] De saeculi nostri felicitate Tibi planissime adsentior. Jactata multa hucusque, nonnulla\n[[333.2]] obiter, nec satis aperto consilio proposita, alia minori certitudine adserta, pleraque curiosiora,\n[[333.3]] quam utiliora, et vetteribus etiam non ignorata. <i>Ephemeridum Germanicarum</i> tomus alter adeo\n[[333.4]] mature prodiit, ut paucula, quae tempori submisi, subjungi non potuerint, in tertium iccirco\n[[333.5]] reservata. Canalis thoracicus cum cavae trunco inferiori communicans, egregium quidem repertum\n[[333.6]] concessero hominis sollertis, sed parum singulare: nam etiam ex trunco inferiori sanguis\n[[333.7]] omnis adscendens, ex artuum et ventris arteriis in venas transsumptus, circulationis nomine non\n[[333.8]] minus ad cor tendit quam descendendo ex arteriis superioribus in venas, et praecipue cavae\n[[333.9]] truncum superiorem, ratione quidem hepatis adscendentem dictum, sed ratione motus potius\n[[333.10]] descendentem dicendum. Cuicunque igitur ramo vas chyliferum inseratur, una cum sanguine\n[[333.11]] chylum ad cor defert in sanguinem elaborandum. </p>\n<p> [[333.12]] Stubbii librum contra Societatem Anglicam et Spratium nondum vidi. Fortasse nec vidisse\n[[333.13]] refert, si contentiosus est. Libros Sinenses multum eruditis profuturos conjicio, sed vereor, ut\n[[333.14]] publicam lucem ocyus subire possint, cum Martinii <i>historia</i> jam dudum promissa necdum\n[[333.15]] compareat. Quid in politicis ab illis exspectandum sit, parum puto, quemadmodum in philosophia\n[[333.16]] universa: si historiam naturalem excipiamus, qua sola Medicinae etiam necessarios\n[[333.17]] existimo. </p>\n<p> [[333.18]] De Menagio olim jam Meibomius ad me scripsit <i>epistola</i> illa, quam <i>de historia Medicorum</i>\n[[333.19]] editam vidisse Te puto. Respondi quidem copiose, sed quod ille optabat, non potui edere,\n[[333.20]] typi Arabici defectu, ideoque hanc curam illi cum jure omni in meam concessi. Si excusam\n[[333.21]] voluerit, facile a Batavis impetrabit, quibus me propior est. Non destiti Bibliothecas omnes\n[[333.22]] sollicitare, quae Mss^#'i^#'s Arabicis celebres aliquid suppeditare possent. Sed parum promovi.\n[[333.23]] Golius petitionem meam cum vita deseruit. Coelestinus frater illius LL. orientalium callentissimus\n[[333.24]] humanissime quidem respondit, sed religiosae vitae negotiis se excusavit, nihil in\n[[333.25]] Vaticana haberi contestatus, quod nobis usui esse possit. Ex Barberina meliora exspectare jubet\n[[333.26]] Moroni benevolentia. Ill^#'i^#'s etiam Lambecius ex Caesarea Vindobonensi quorundam Codicum\n[[333.27]] usum concessit, si cautionem praestiterim intra certum tempus restituendi. Quod cum aequissimum\n[[333.28]] sit, non videtur tamen mihi privati hominis esse summo Monarchae cautionem praestare.\n[[333.29]] Ideoque de potentioris alicujus gratia nunc cogito, qui favorem suum interponat. </p>\n<p> [[334.1]] <i>Hypothesin</i> Tuam de motu lucis circa terram vidi, nec displicet. Si tamen Digbaei\n[[334.2]] sententiae accedis, qui sympathiam unguenti armarii et pulv. sympathetici dicti ex illa deduxit,\n[[334.3]] cogitandum Tibi saltem intelliges, quid Deusingio responderi possit, qui curationis illius ludibrium\n[[334.4]] mascule oppugnavit. De recipiente Magdeburgico nulla apud me est memoria. Si quid\n[[334.5]] scitu dignum suggerat, quaeso mone. De acido et alcali nolim Te chemicorum more valde\n[[334.6]] sollicitum esse. Est enim illorum actio in multis quidem manifesta. Sed ex ipso nomine facile\n[[334.7]] capies, acidum proprie salino non opponi. Nec enim aliud alcali significat, quam sal fixum.\n[[334.8]] Atqui nec acida omnia volatilia sunt, nec quae sunt, propterea non salina sunt, multoque magis\n[[334.9]] acida, quae fixa sunt. Ludunt nos qui haec talia ubique crepant. Werneri machina aquaria non\n[[334.10]] contemnenda, nec tamen tanti facienda est, quanti videtur. Facilis est, et nihil habet <greek>tṽn\n[[334.11]] ădynátvn.</greek> </p>\n<p> [[334.12]] Exercitationem meam <i>de Vena Medinensi</i> Typochyta Francofurtensis etiamnum remoratur,\n[[334.13]] qui tot annis jam Arabica nobis debet. Totus nunc occupor in Sim. Sethi recensendo, quem\n[[334.14]] geminae editioni et tribus Mss^#'i^#'s contuli. Accepi etiam varias lectiones ex Mediolanensi Ambrosiana,\n[[334.15]] aliasque Oxonio exspecto a Cl^#'s^#'s^#'o Hydeo ex Bodleiana. Lindeni praeterea notas cum variis\n[[334.16]] Leonis Allatii ex Vaticana a Rhodio quondam impetratas Henricus filius Amstelodamo submisit\n[[334.17]] Exc^#'s^#'s^#'o Bacmestero procurante. Infinitas Tibi gratias debebit orbis literatus Universus, si Abulfeda\n[[334.18]] Schiccardi Tua cura tandem prodierit. Patere tamen, obsecro, ut Te exorem, ne Arabica\n[[334.19]] omittantur. Etsi enim optima fuerit versio, quod credere par est, multum tamen auctoritatis\n[[334.20]] necessariae a textu ipso accedet. </p>\n<p> [[334.21]] Vedelii <i>sal volatile</i> novum non est, utut forsan modus conficiendi novus sit. Nemo haec\n[[334.22]] talia inter Medicos jam olim ignorat. Imperitis nebulae offunduntur ejusmodi promissis, de\n[[335.1]] quibus tamen nihil decerno, quia necdum vidi. Ludovici autem Gothani <i>pharmaceutica</i> attente\n[[335.2]] evolvi, et animadversiones extemporales adscripsi meis usibus. Laudo viri adfectum de publico\n[[335.3]] bene merendi, sed nimia severitas illius et simplicium amor desperabilis, una cum stylo nescio\n[[335.4]] quid pomposi adfectante, ac ideo ea in re, quae summam lucem poscit, obscuro, non satis ad\n[[335.5]] ingenium meum facit. De Societate Panctetica Venetiis per amicos inquiram. Vereor autem, ut\n[[335.6]] illa Solis amicitia parum absit a Chrysomania, quam nonnemo delirii alchymistici nomine\n[[335.7]] etiam medicamentis curandam docuit. Molinettus propediem Patavii alteram <i>de organis sensuum</i>\n[[335.8]] partem editurus est. Ferrarius sua de lucernis et toga nondum absolvit. Ursatus Eques\n[[335.9]] inscriptiones antiquas ad me misit, quas nondum obtinui. </p>\n<p> [[335.10]] Si liceat, proximis locum ex Pandectis de rebus vectigalibus Tibi repraesentabo, quo mihi\n[[335.11]] cum opus sit, et tamen non satis sanum deprehendam, emendationem meam Tuo judicio\n[[335.12]] subjiciam, non temere, ut puto, quia non omnino a Jurisprudentia alienus, cui nunc animum\n[[335.13]] addixi, quod credam neminem unum vere doctum aut sapientem dici posse, qui illam ignoret.\n[[335.14]] Si monueris et correxeris, gratissimam rem feceris, multumque Tibi me devinxeris, nec ego\n[[335.15]] publice aliquando reticebo. </p>\n<p> [[335.16]] Vale, et amorem Tuum mihi perpetuum serva, qui nominis Tui amplitudini et virtutibus\n[[335.17]] singularibus addictissimus ero, dum vixero. D. Augustae Vindelicorum MDCLXXII. XIV. Idus\n[[335.18]] Aprilis. </p>\n<p> [[335.19]] Viro Nob^#'s^#'s^#'o Ampl^#'s^#'s^#'o atque Excell^#'s^#'s^#'o Gothofredo Guilelmo Leibnizio U.J.D. praeclarissimo,\n[[335.20]] Dⁿ^#'o et Fautori meo honoratissimo. Moguntiam.\n [[335.21]] 106. LEIBNIZ AN ─ (?)\n<p> [[335.22]] 1667 ─ 1672.</b> jetzt N. 95a.</p>\n[[337.1]] <b>II. PARIS März 1672 ─ November 1676</b> </p>\n",
  "number": "105.",
  "title": "GEORG HIERONYMUS WELSCH AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Augsburg, [April] 1672."
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:105. GEORG HIERONYMUS WELSCH AN LEIBNIZ Augsburg, [April] 1672. Viro Nobil^#'s^#'s^#'o Ampl^#'s^#'s^#'o atque Excell^#'s^#'s^#'o Gothofredo Guilelmo Leibnizio U.J.D. praeclar^#'s^#'s^#'o, Dⁿ^#'o et Fautori suo plurimum honorando, Georgius Hieronymus Velschius S.P.D. Fecisti sane, Vir Nobil^#'s^#'s^#...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>